  "narrative": "These 12 results test stability of the central accepted feature_021-outcome_006 association and screen for a new outcome_006 categorical marker. For outcome_006, I use the same approximate clinical threshold used throughout the run, about 0.0093 absolute units, corresponding to 10% of the outcome_006 mean magnitude near 0.093. The five direct binary-modifier interactions H114-H118 all fail to support a clinically meaningful positive modification of the accepted feature_021=1 versus feature_021=0 effect. H114, H116, H117, and H130 have point estimates in the opposite direction from the claimed positive interaction. H115 and H118 have positive point estimates above the clinical threshold, but their intervals include zero, clinically negligible modification, and clinically meaningful values in the opposite direction. Because acceptance requires evidence that the positive interaction exceeds the clinical threshold, and because these interaction tests are diagnostic refinements rather than central claims, I reject these positive interaction claims and close them. This does not prove exact zero interaction; it means the present data do not support clinically meaningful positive modification. These results strengthen the interpretation that the central +0.80 feature_021-outcome_006 association is stable across the tested common binary modifiers, at least within the precision available from direct Welch-subgroup contrasts.\n\nThe categorical marker screens show mostly nonclinical or uncertain positive top-level associations. H120 is negative rather than positive. H121, H122, and H123 have intervals that include null and clinically negligible differences; H123 is below threshold even at the point estimate. Therefore I reject their positive clinical-effect claims and close them. The median-split interaction H129 is also below threshold and uncertain, and H130 is opposite direction; both are rejected and closed.\n\nH119 is the one scientifically important exception. The signed positive estimate for outcome_006 comparing feature_009 level_003 with level_001 is +0.0513, about 5.5 times the approximate 10% threshold of 0.0093. However, the 95% interval is -0.0017 to +0.1042, so the lower bound remains just below zero and therefore does not establish a clinically meaningful positive association beyond reasonable uncertainty. This is not strong enough to accept as a new marker, but it is much more suggestive than the other screens and would materially expand the current two-marker landscape if independently supported. The comparator cell is relatively small (n=175), so wide uncertainty is plausible. Because independent validation is useful and we still have validation capacity, I keep H119 unresolved and request validation of H119. If validation confirms a large positive feature_009 level_003 effect on outcome_006, I will need follow-up specificity and independence checks, especially against the accepted feature_021 marker and across other outcomes. If validation is near null or subclinical, I will reject and close H119 and retain the central supplied-dataset conclusion as two large marker-like associations, feature_021-outcome_006 and feature_027-outcome_014.",
