on. H155 tests analogous modification of feature_027 on outcome_014; R149 is -0.0070 with CI [-0.0473, +0.0334]. These are consistent with stability of the two central associations rather than evidence for a clinically meaningful subgroup modification.\n\nThe final broad binary screens H132-H136 all fail to support claimed positive associations for outcome_013, outcome_008, outcome_011, and outcome_001 with feature_034 or feature_002. R150 through R154 all have signed point estimates below or opposite the relevant benchmarks and intervals crossing zero or negligible values. I reject and close H132, H133, H134, H135, and H136. These nulls make a new broad binary marker unlikely, though they do not prove absence for every untested predictor.\n\nIn the modifier family for the accepted feature_021-outcome_006 association, H126 is rejected: R156 is -0.0024 with CI [-0.0511, +0.0464], far from a supportable positive modification. H124 is the only new nondecisive signal: R155 is +0.0289 with CI [-0.0150, +0.0728], a positive point above the outcome_006 benchmark but an interval that still includes zero, negligible modification, and clinically meaningful opposite modification. I leave H124 unresolved rather than accepted or fully closed because it is a potential modifier of a large supported marker effect. However, I do not request validation for it yet: its prior is weakened by the failed independent validation of the related feature_009 main-effect lead H119, by the large number of interaction screens, and by the very wide discovery interval. An independent validation at the stringent run-wide alpha may not resolve it unless the true modification is much larger than currently estimated. I activate H125, H127, and H128 to complete the same feature_021 interaction family; if those are null, H124 will be much more plausibly a chance lead and should be closed. If any produces a robust positive interval beyond benchmark, I will use validation capacity on that stronger candidate. The supported supplied-dataset landscape remains unchanged: feature_021=1 is associated with much higher outcome_006 scores, and feature_027=1 is associated with much higher outcome_014 scores. These are dataset-internal associations only, not causal or externally generalizable claims.",
